    "content": "Amazon does not offer a specific, age-based discount for seniors. However, seniors receiving government assistance (Medicaid, SNAP, SSI, etc.) qualify for Prime Access, which costs $6.99 per month—over 50% off the standard $14.99 rate. Without qualifying for assistance, seniors pay the standard $14.99 monthly or $139 annually. Prime Access Key Details for Seniors: Eligibility: To get the $6.99 rate, you must verify eligibility for programs like Medicaid, SNAP, or SSI using an EBT card or other documentation on the Prime Access page. Prime Access page Benefits: Prime Access includes all standard Prime benefits, such as free shipping, Prime Video, and savings on groceries. Re-verification: Eligibility must be verified every 12 months. Trial Period: New Prime Access members receive a 30-day free trial. Standard Rate: If not eligible for assistance, the cost is the standard $14.99 per month or $139 per year. Note: SSDI (Social Security Disability Insurance) does not qualify for this discount, while SSI (Supplemental Security Income) does.",
